    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nHi!\r\nI'm a long time vim-surround user, so I wanted to change the mappings of mini.surround to reflect those present in vim-surround. In that plugin, you use `ys` to add a surrounding. This remapping fine in normal mode, but when highlighting something in visual mode and pressing `y` to yank it, it puts you in operator pending mode - presumably because it's waiting to see if you want to execute `ys` from mini.surround.\r\n\r\nI'd really like a way to map only for normal mode. For inspiration, vim-surround maps `S` to add a surrounding when in visual mode.\r\n\r\nI've also remapped changing a surrounding to `cs`. Curiously, pressing `c` when in visual mode does not put you in operator pending.\r\n\r\nPlease let me know if anything is unclear, or if you'd like a minimal config to try it out and compare with vim-surround.\r\n\r\nThanks for this great plugin!",
    "closed_at": "2022-04-26T10:41:26Z",
