        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion and kind words!\r\n\r\nYou've got a valid point here. I was a 'vim-sandwich' user myself, so an overall design is more adapted towards it. I am leaning towards adding this, but I tend to spend at least a night before making such decision. Tomorrow I hope to get back here.\r\n\r\nTwo nitpicks:\r\n- In your case after pressing `y` in Visual mode Neovim doesn't \"go into Operator pending mode\". It waits `timeoutlen` time for a possible mapping to complete. So basically everything you said, but without \"Operator pending mode\" name.\r\n- There is no such behavior for `cs` and `c` in Visual mode because there is no mapping for \"change surrounding\" in Visual mode.",
